      "input": "\"Which of you is captain here?\" I ask the guards, looking from one face to the other.",
      "output": "The North Gate arches over me, its stonework weathered by centuries of wind and foot traffic. I pause, eyes sweeping across the gatehouse with its heavy timbers and iron fittings, the handful of guards on duty in their worn leather and steel, and the bustling Market Square that opens beyond the open doorway.\n\nNoise spills through from the square, voices and cart wheels and the clatter of goods. The air carries a faint tang of woodsmoke and damp earth. I stand there a moment longer, then speak it.\n\nThe words cut across the guards. One meets my gaze squarely while the other glances aside; my look travels from one face to the other and finds only guarded silence in return.",
